t","text":" instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A transition leading back to the same state delivers the state again."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A rejected event delivers nothing, as the state machine stays where it is."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call creates a new stream, independent of all other streams."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Several consumers can each have a stream of their own, and all of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them get every state. Cancelling the task of a consumer, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"letting go of a stream, ends only that stream."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The stream finishes when the state machine reaches an ending state,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after delivering that state. A stream created at an ending state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivers the state and finishes. The stream also finishes if the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state machine is deallocated.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/MiamiStateMachine\/documentation\/MiamiStateMachine\/StateMachine\/stateStream(bufferingPolicy:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MiamiStateMachine\/documentation\/MiamiStateMachine","doc:\/\/MiamiStateMachine\/documentation\/MiamiStateMachine\/StateMachine"]]},"references":{"doc://MiamiStateMachine/documentation/MiamiStateMachine/StateMachine/stateStream(bufferingPolicy:)":{"type":"topic","title":"stateStream(bufferingPolicy:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a stream of the states the state machine is at. It starts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"with the current state, followed by the state entered by every","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"transition made from now on, in the ord